if you think we need animal protein to  thrive think again  gone are the days of strict dietary  requirements we live in the age of  nutritional choices based on a person's  biochemical individuality in other words  choose the foods that work best for your  body today on million ways to live we  spend the day with a rich role one of  the fittest men on the planet who went  against all mainstream marketing and  hype and shut his critics up by  listening to the innate wisdom of his  own body  through trial and error rich learned  that the optimal fuel for his mind and  body was one based on vegan principles  since then he has conquered the ultraman  challenge a grueling three-day 320 mile  endurance race and followed it up with  the epic five challenge completing five  Ironman triathlons on five different  Hawaiian Islands in less than a week my  journey towards eating plant-based was  kind of an easy decision because at the  time my wife was already vegetarian I  knew she was healthy and I wasn't so it  was an easy decision to jump on the  Household bandwagon first thing I did  was a juice fast which was cruelly and  brutal and painful it was very much like  coming off drugs and at the time I  didn't think that my junk food habit was  an addiction until I felt those  withdrawal symptoms but once the fog  cleared I knew I was never going back to  my old way of life because I'd never  experienced such levels of clarity and  energy and focus before and the next  question of course is what are you gonna  eat now I decided to adopt a vegetarian  diet but I quickly realized that just  because I was vegetarian that that did  not necessarily mean that I was healthy  there are plenty of unhealthy vegetarian  and vegan junk foods out there and  believe me I ate all of them thinking I  was healthy french fries potato chips  vegan cupcakes pancakes even Oreos are  technically vegan after about six months  of being a junk food vegetarian I had  played it out I was back on the couch I  hadn't lost any weight my energy levels  had plummeted again and I thought what  would happen if I got rid of all the  processed foods what would happen if I  got rid of all the dairy products what  would happen if I went 100% entirely a  food plant-based once I started looking  past the labels and choosing high  quality nutrient-dense superfoods like  quinoa and avocados started embracing a  diet rich in fruits and vegetables my  energy levels were stored and I felt  like I did in the latter days of that  juice cleanse  I was so energized I had to go outside  and start exercising again even though  the triathlon is an individual event  rich knows that a supporting cast is the  most important part of any successful  venture  for rich there's no one more important  to his team than his wife Julie my  greatest enemy has always been me left  to my own devices I will generally  self-sabotage any effort towards getting  healthy but I'm lucky enough to be  married to Julie and Julie has always  been my rock she provides me  unconditional love and support and she's  also been an amazing teacher introducing  me to things like meditation yoga things  that are rejuvenating my body after  intense training days life is about  balance everything Julie is and stands  for represents that balance for me good  things don't come easy starting at  Ground Zero rich pushed his body to  levels only few humans have ever  experienced milestones like that don't  just happen overnight  trying to find efficiencies and ways to  streamline your life is fine there's  nothing wrong with that but I do have a  problem when the hacking the life  hacking the bio hacking becomes the  destination rather than a tool hacks may  trick the human mind into thinking  something has been accomplished but you  can't trick the body your body is  constantly adapting to the environment  you place it in and a quick hack simply  is not going to offset years of bad  habits rather than focusing on shortcuts  and hacks do the internal work to find  out what makes your heart beat parties  when you find your purpose and calling  follow it with all of your heart and  soul I've got to stick with it and if  you do you'll find that your journey  will be the most amazing adventure you  can possibly imagine
 

